WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.715
Beyond bloom and color, Geometry and Post FX change the whole character of the beam.

2
00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:08.668
Geometry sets how the raster is drawn.

3
00:00:08.668 --> 00:00:10.774
Wireframe makes it a solid mesh.

4
00:00:10.774 --> 00:00:12.947
Dot Raster draws only the points.

5
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.014
Custom Tint picks any phosphor color you like.

6
00:00:16.014 --> 00:00:17.208
Magenta, for a start.

7
00:00:17.663 --> 00:00:19.490
Burn-In Feedback leaves trails.

8
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.380
Its shape can be a circle, so only the middle of the frame smears.

9
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.325
Move the camera to paint with it.

10
00:00:28.087 --> 00:00:32.916
Analog Character adds grain, dropouts and a rolling hum bar, like a tired old monitor.

11
00:00:38.069 --> 00:00:41.330
Chromatic aberration splits the colors at the edges.

12
00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:44.152
Scanlines and a vignette finish the CRT look.

13
00:00:44.781 --> 00:00:49.525
Each effect has its own on switch, and every slider can be modulated.

14
00:00:49.525 --> 00:00:51.932
Next: saving and sharing your work.
